# Neighboring texts of a concatenation are joined by new values, and making a value may move the concatenation. Each function makes more values than the last one, so that one of them moves it. Under the address sanitizer a read of the old place is an error.
# FORM: Prepared
# RUN: pass FuseConcatenations

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
function f0 name="join1" parameters=[{type=string}] results=[{type=anything}] {
    v1 = String string="a0"
    v2 = String string="b0"
    v3 = Strcat v0, v1, v2, v0
    Return v3
# CHECK: "a0b0" = String string="a0b0"
# CHECK-NOT: = String string="a0"
}

